VulkanOptics (optics::)
======================

Reusable Vulkan material compositor. The host owns rasterization,
G-buffers, swapchain, photon-transport lifetime and command buffers.
No hardware ray-tracing extensions, cubemap/probe substitutes or second BVH.

Reflective and glass faces are removed from the opaque G-buffer and
composited from a separate front-surface material target. One shared
software BVH traces ordered secondary hits through glass, other mirrors
and ordinary geometry. Bounded ray-path branching handles Fresnel
reflection and straight-through thin-glass transmission, with
no compiler-side shader recursion. Glass does not bend viewing rays
or magnify the background; tint and Fresnel reflection remain.

Reflected/through-glass GLB base-color textures are sampled via a GPU
RGBA8 texture atlas plus per-face triangle UV mappings. Alpha-cutout
textures are also tested during BVH intersections. The host supplies
the decoded textures and UVs using compositor::set_textures(). Textures
are packed with 1-pixel duplicated borders and uploaded only when the
streamed scene changes; a single atlas is bounded at 8192x8192 pixels.

When an opaque hit is directly camera-visible, its fully lit rasterized
pixel is sampled, preserving material and animation details. Otherwise
the BVH hit is shaded from its source texture, procedural checker material,
scene lights and the existing photon-grid radiance. No shifted
screen-image refraction is performed, preventing duplicate first-person
weapons. Viewmodel geometry is not included in the world BVH.

Individual photon deposits are NOT displayed. Photon data remains an
invisible indirect-lighting cache for shading reflected off-screen hits.
The optics compositor does not modify ordinary scene lighting based on
glass transmission or mirror reflections: there is no color spill, caustic
projection, or additional full-screen material-lighting correction.
The optional caustics projector is not called by VulkanGame.

Known limitations: CPU-built Photon Mapping BVH positions currently
represent the streamed mesh at its static/bind pose, not live skinned
vertices. Off-screen point-light shading does not yet match every
material channel of the primary PCloud renderer (e.g. metallic-roughness
and normal maps). View-dependent recursion is bounded to 10 surface
interactions; large mirror coverage needs further profiling. The
texture atlas has a finite 8192x8192 upper bound. Performance
optimizations are deferred until image correctness is validated on M2.

Public API: optics/optics.hpp, optics/caustics.hpp.
Shaders: optics/shaders/compose.frag, raytrace.glsl.
